  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#PowerBidDependency">
    <cims:belongsToCategory rdf:resource="https://ap-voc.cim4.eu/StateInstructionSchedule#StateInstructionScheduleProfile"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A peer temporal dependency that defines temporal or operational constraints between two power bid schedules.
Note: The dependency constrains activation or deactivation of the dependent power bid schedule relative to activation or deactivation of the dependee power bid schedule. Lag constraints are evaluated from the latest applicable activation or deactivation of the dependee. A subsequent state change of the dependee supersedes the previous reference transition if the corresponding transition of the dependent has not yet occurred.
Example:
- startToStartLag = 15M, startToStartLagKind = exact: the dependent bid is activated exactly 15 minutes after activation of the dependee bid, provided the dependee has not subsequently changed state.
- finishToStartLag = 30M, finishToStartLagKind = minimum: the dependent bid may be activated no earlier than 30 minutes after deactivation of the dependee bid.
- finishToFinishLag = 15M, finishToFinishLagKind = maximum: the dependent bid shall be deactivated no later than 15 minutes after deactivation of the dependee bid.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PowerBidDependency</rdfs:label>
    <cims:stereotype>NC</cims:stereotype>
    <cims:stereotype rdf:resource="http://iec.ch/TC57/NonStandard/UML#concrete"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#PeerTemporalDependency"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#PowerBidSchedule">
    <cims:belongsToCategory rdf:resource="https://ap-voc.cim4.eu/StateInstructionSchedule#StateInstructionScheduleProfile"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Power bid or offer related to a redispatch or countertrading measures. In the case of market place for economic efficiency of the bids and offers, this is equivalent to BidTimeSeries class in 62325 package.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PowerBidSchedule</rdfs:label>
    <cims:stereotype>NC</cims:stereotype>
    <cims:stereotype rdf:resource="http://iec.ch/TC57/NonStandard/UML#concrete"/>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#BaseIrregularTimeSeries"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#PowerBidScheduleTimePoint">
    <cims:belongsToCategory rdf:resource="https://ap-voc.cim4.eu/StateInstructionSchedule#StateInstructionScheduleProfile"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Time series represent irregular values at given points in time.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PowerBidScheduleTimePoint</rdfs:label>
    <cims:stereotype>NC</cims:stereotype>
    <cims:stereotype rdf:resource="http://iec.ch/TC57/NonStandard/UML#concrete"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="#PowerElectronicsUnit">
    <cims:belongsToCategory rdf:resource="https://ap-voc.cim4.eu/StateInstructionSchedule#StateInstructionScheduleProfile"/>
    <rdfs:comment>A generating unit or battery or aggregation that connects to the AC network using power electronics rather than rotating machines.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PowerElectronicsUnit</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#PowerFactorControlFunction">
    <cims:belongsToCategory rdf:resource="https://ap-voc.cim4.eu/StateInstructionSchedule#StateInstructionScheduleProfile"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Power factor control function is a function block that calculates the operating point of the controlled equipment to achieve the target power factor.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">PowerFactorControlFunction</rdfs:label>
    <cims:stereotype>NC</cims:stereotype>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Class"/>
