    <rdfs:comment>Day of the week other than Sunday or Saturday.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">weekday</rdfs:label>
    <cims:stereotype>enum</cims:stereotype>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#DayOfWeekKind"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#DayOfWeekKind.weekend">
    <rdfs:comment>Day of the week which is Sunday or Saturday.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">weekend</rdfs:label>
    <cims:stereotype>enum</cims:stereotype>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#DayOfWeekKind"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#DependencyConstraintKind.exclusive">
    <rdfs:comment>The dependee and dependent shall not both be active or effective at the same time.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">exclusive</rdfs:label>
    <cims:stereotype>enum</cims:stereotype>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#DependencyConstraintKind"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#DependencyConstraintKind.inclusive">
    <rdfs:comment>The dependent shall only be active or effective while the dependee is active or effective.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">inclusive</rdfs:label>
    <cims:stereotype>enum</cims:stereotype>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#DependencyConstraintKind"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#DependencyConstraintKind.restrictive">
    <rdfs:comment>The dependee constrains the dependent without requiring the dependent to become active or effective.
Note: A restrictive dependency defines temporal or operational constraints on the behaviour of the dependent while leaving its activation or operation optional.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">restrictive</rdfs:label>
    <cims:stereotype>enum</cims:stereotype>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#DependencyConstraintKind"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#EnergyScenarioKind.consumption">
    <rdfs:comment>Scenario focus on consumption of energy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">consumption</rdfs:label>
    <cims:stereotype>enum</cims:stereotype>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#EnergyScenarioKind"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#EnergyScenarioKind.export">
    <rdfs:comment>Scenario focus on export of energy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">export</rdfs:label>
    <cims:stereotype>enum</cims:stereotype>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#EnergyScenarioKind"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#EnergyScenarioKind.import">
    <rdfs:comment>Scenario focus on import of energy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">import</rdfs:label>
    <cims:stereotype>enum</cims:stereotype>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#EnergyScenarioKind"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#EnergyScenarioKind.production">
    <rdfs:comment>Scenario focus on production of energy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">production</rdfs:label>
    <cims:stereotype>enum</cims:stereotype>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#EnergyScenarioKind"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#EnergyScenarioKind.storage">
    <rdfs:comment>Scenario focus on storage of energy.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">storage</rdfs:label>
    <cims:stereotype>enum</cims:stereotype>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#EnergyScenarioKind"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#MarketRegulationDirectionKind.down">
    <rdfs:comment>Regulation activation that decreases the system’s net power injection — achieved either by decreasing generation or increasing consumption. Used for down-regulation bids or activations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">down</rdfs:label>
    <cims:stereotype>enum</cims:stereotype>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#MarketRegulationDirectionKind"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#MarketRegulationDirectionKind.stable">
    <rdfs:comment>No activation or neutral position; used for capacity or reserve states that maintain stability without a directional effect (e.g., system in balanced or standby mode).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">stable</rdfs:label>
    <cims:stereotype>enum</cims:stereotype>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#MarketRegulationDirectionKind"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#MarketRegulationDirectionKind.up">
    <rdfs:comment>Regulation activation that increases the system’s net power injection — achieved either by increasing generation or decreasing consumption. Used for up-regulation bids or activations.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">up</rdfs:label>
    <cims:stereotype>enum</cims:stereotype>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#MarketRegulationDirectionKind"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#MarketRegulationDirectionKind.upAndDown">
    <rdfs:comment>Product or capacity symmetrical for both up- and down-regulation; the same magnitude applies in both directions. Common for bidirectional balancing services (e.g., symmetrical aFRR capacity).</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">upAndDown</rdfs:label>
    <cims:stereotype>enum</cims:stereotype>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#MarketRegulationDirectionKind"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#PeakKind.offPeak">
    <rdfs:comment>Off-peak refer to periods of lower demand for a particular service or commodity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">offPeak</rdfs:label>
    <cims:stereotype>enum</cims:stereotype>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#PeakKind"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#PeakKind.onPeak">
    <rdfs:comment>Off-peak refer to periods of higher demand for a particular service or commodity.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">onPeak</rdfs:label>
    <cims:stereotype>enum</cims:stereotype>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://cim4.eu/ns/nc#PeakKind"/>
  </rdf:Description>
